  "description": "AJOWIG crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C65 H133 Dy4 Fe7 N7 O44 1+,N1 O3 1-,3(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Fe1 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe3 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe4 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Fe5 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Fe6 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe7 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 29 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.947-3.955 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.49-134.64°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Fe7Dy4O4(OH)3(tea)2(Htea)3(Piv)7(NO3)2(H2O)2](NO3)·3MeCN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 tea (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 Htea (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 7 Piv (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 tea (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 Htea (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 7 Piv (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Fe(III), Dy(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
